## Scoring Instructions

Evaluate the candidate across the following 8 dimensions. Each dimension has a maximum score (points) and sub-criteria with percentage weights within that dimension.

### 1. skillsMatch (Max: {{ weights_skills_match }} pts)
- Must-Have Skills Coverage (60%): How many MUST_HAVE skills does the candidate demonstrably possess? Look for direct mentions, project usage, and certifications.
- Nice-to-Have Skills Coverage (20%): Coverage of NICE_TO_HAVE skills.
- Skill Depth & Recency (20%): Are skills used recently and at depth (not just listed)?

### 2. experienceRelevance (Max: {{ weights_experience_relevance }} pts)
- Total Years Match (40%): Does the candidate's total experience match the JD requirements?
- Relevant Experience (35%): How much of their experience is directly relevant to this role?
- Career Progression (25%): Does their career show logical growth toward this role?

### 3. projectRelevance (Max: {{ weights_project_relevance }} pts)
- Domain-Matching Projects (40%): Projects in the same domain or solving similar problems.
- Tech Stack Alignment (27%): Projects using the required tech stack.
- Scale & Impact (20%): Evidence of working at relevant scale (team size, users, data volume).
- Innovation (13%): Unique or innovative contributions.

### 4. educationCertifications (Max: {{ weights_education_certifications }} pts)
- Degree Match (40%): Relevant degree level and field of study.
- Institution Quality (30%): Quality/reputation of educational institutions.
- Certifications (20%): Relevant professional certifications.
- Continuous Learning (10%): Evidence of ongoing learning (courses, workshops, conferences).

### 5. domainIndustryFit (Max: {{ weights_domain_industry_fit }} pts)
- Same Industry Experience (50%): Has the candidate worked in the same or closely related industry?
- Domain Tools & Methodologies (30%): Familiarity with domain-specific tools and practices.
- Client/Customer Segment (20%): Experience with similar client segments or market.

### 6. roleSeniorityFit (Max: {{ weights_role_seniority_fit }} pts)
- Title Alignment (50%): How closely does their current/recent title match the target role level?
- Scope of Responsibility (25%): Does their responsibility scope match what's expected?
- Management/Leadership Span (25%): Appropriate people/project management experience for the role level.

### 7. culturalSoftSignals (Max: {{ weights_cultural_soft_signals }} pts)
- Communication Signals (29%): Evidence of strong communication (presentations, publications, cross-team work).
- Leadership Indicators (29%): Mentoring, initiative-taking, thought leadership.
- Collaboration Evidence (28%): Cross-functional work, team contributions, open source.
- Values Alignment (14%): Any signals of alignment with company values or mission.

### 8. logisticsAvailability (Max: {{ weights_logistics_availability }} pts)
- Location Fit (40%): Is the candidate in or willing to relocate to the right location?
- Work Model Compatibility (20%): Remote/hybrid/on-site preference alignment.
- Notice Period (20%): Availability timeline (if mentioned).
- Compensation Alignment (20%): Any salary/compensation signals that align.

## Verdict Scale
- EXCELLENT_FIT: Total score 85-100
- STRONG_FIT: Total score 70-84
- GOOD_FIT: Total score 55-69
- PARTIAL_FIT: Total score 40-54
- WEAK_FIT: Total score 0-39

